{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1236530-personality-for-shocking-characters","id":1236530,"title":"Personality for shocking characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-18T13:16:17-07:00","id":1236530,"title":"Personality for shocking characters?","content":"This is a very general question and so to the general area it goes. As a fan of a lot of the darker things in WoD, I often run into examples of character splats that seem flat and uninspired. Cenobite aping Tzimisce being the best example of a typical character trope I am referring to.<br /> <br /> So, those who play your Tzimisce/Nephandi/Salubri/BSDs,etc, how do you make sure your character isn't just a vehicle for gore and horror and nothing else? What makes them, maybe not human, but a person beyond their splat?<br /> <br /> For me, the general rule is twisted morality and things the character considers heinous. Maybe they are extremely protective of their family, or maybe they hold some things sacred to themselves. I try to avoid these things being related to their splat or to their species culture, because I feel having an actually positive aspect to the character helps to balance out the horror and give a sense that the character is capable of more than violence. Which makes their willing deeds all the more horrifying in contrast.<br /> <br /> If the character never had a choice, I try to portray the cracks in the monster facade. The person that still exist under the gore and how they have morphed their empathy and love to fit their world. The important thing is that it is faulty and awkward, because those skills are underdeveloped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T16:29:50-07:00","id":1236940,"title":"","content":"There is a Monster Nature in a few of the core books for unrepentant Monsters, but I think every character created needs a reason to progress the plot and try to work with the rest of the Pack/Coterie/Cabal/Whatever","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T17:08:56-07:00","id":1236955,"title":"","content":"I had a Tzimisce once, granted he was Old Clan and was a Kuldonic Sorceror, but still a Tzimisce to the core and quite, unhuman, so to speak. An Old World Noble from a long line of Noble, there were no human emotion or compassion anymore and couldn't care less about what year or century he was in. He was your social better and you better damn act accordingly and he would not abide by any breach of the proper protocol of his people.<br /> <br /> When approached the correct way, he could be quite agreeable and he was a strong believer of Hospitality and the covenant that came with it too. Depending on how you approach him, he could be your greatest ally or your worse enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 07-22-2018, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T17:24:45-07:00","id":1236957,"title":"","content":"That's something I really like about Dark ages and the Sabbat, you can portray inhuman meaning not-human not just anti-humanity. Reasonable individuals in the right circumstances with consistent morality (Even if it's a personal one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatar